 ### SCENARIO-PHASE4-083: Exp4351 Banks New Reproduced Deeper Levels Or Records Honest Per-Target Partials
 **Description:** Running Exp 4351 either writes `success_e3_deeper_<targets>_reproduced` when at least one target independently reproduces a new level beyond its prior best via `arc_solver_kit.reproduce()`, or writes `complete_e3_deeper_partial` when all available targets complete their bounded checkpoint attempts without a new reproduced level. A successful run MUST set `new_levels_reproduced>=1`, `reproducible_total_levels>=21`, `verifier_is_oracle=true`, include exactly one `per_target_scorecard` row for each of `sc25`, `tn36`, and `ar25`, preserve `world_model_paths`, set `submitted_to_leaderboard=false`, and compute the reproducibility checksum from the target rows, deliverable hashes, plans, reproduction-gate results, and random seed. A partial run MUST preserve the same scorecard shape, set `offline_reproduced=false` for targets that did not advance beyond their prior best, record each target's best verifier accuracy and residual win-mechanic gap class, and record any missing environment as `blocked_offline_env_missing_<game>` without blocking the remaining targets.
+
+### REQ-PHASE4-084: ARC-AGI-3 E3 Explore-Verify-Plan tr87 And ft09 Exp4352
+**Description:** The system SHALL run Exp 4352 as an offline, no-leaderboard continuation over `tr87` and `ft09`, applying the explore-verify-plan harness upgrade that reproduced `ar25` and `sc25` L1 after the Exp 4329 partial models. It MUST checkpoint `tr87` before `ft09`, first confirm each offline environment under `environment_files/<game>/` is non-empty, confirm `python/carnot/agentic/arc_executable_world_model.py` and `python/carnot/agentic/arc_solver_kit.py` import, confirm TRM training is stood down, and MUST NOT modify `scripts/research_conductor.py` or submit to the leaderboard. If a game's offline environment is missing, it MUST record `blocked_offline_env_missing_<game>` for that game and continue the other. For each available game it MUST use `results/arc_e3/<game>/world_model.py` as the induced deliverable, collect offline transitions, run bounded AERA-style verifier-gated exploration and Agent2World-style adaptive hidden-rule tests, print and persist per-round verifier accuracy, plan only after the mechanic checks pass, and accept progress only when `arc_solver_kit.reproduce()` reports `reproduced=true` with `reached_level>=1`. If the bounded per-game budget ends without a reproduced L1, it MUST write an honest partial row with the best verifier accuracy and residual mismatch class as a missing-world-model-rule gap. The terminal artifact `results/experiment_4352_e3_explore_verify_plan_tr87_ft09.json` MUST include `honest_verdict`, `per_game_scorecard`, `world_model_paths`, `new_levels_reproduced`, `verifier_is_oracle`, `preconditions_checked`, `random_seed`, and `reproducibility_checksum`, with `new_levels_reproduced` and `verifier_is_oracle` emitted as bare values rather than principle-wrapped dictionaries. The artifact field principles SHALL be exactly: `honest_verdict` = `Terminal-prefixed (success_e3_tr87_ft09_<n>_reproduced or complete_e3_tr87_ft09_partial). Any reproduced L1 and an honest partial per game are BOTH progress.`; `per_game_scorecard` = `list of {game, verifier_accuracy, offline_reproduced, reproduced_levels} -- the breadth-of-progress record for tr87/ft09.`; `world_model_paths` = `list[str]: results/arc_e3/{tr87,ft09}/world_model.py -- the induced models ARE the deliverables.`; `new_levels_reproduced` = `BARE int: NEW levels offline-reproduced across tr87+ft09 -- the incremental-progress unit.`; `verifier_is_oracle` = `BARE bool=true -- the SOLVEs are execution-grounded; ARC progress, NOT a moat headline.`; `preconditions_checked` = `Records the offline-env presence per game + harness import + TRM-stand-down; pre-empts the silent-missing-resource fabrication mode.`; `random_seed` = `Determinism precondition for the induction + exploration + planning.`; `reproducibility_checksum` = `Hash of the world models + the plans + the reproduce() results; lets a third party re-run.`
+
+### SCENARIO-PHASE4-084: Exp4352 Reproduces tr87 Or ft09 L1 Or Records Honest Partials
+**Description:** Running Exp 4352 either writes `success_e3_tr87_ft09_<n>_reproduced` when one or both games independently satisfy `offline_reproduced=true` and `reproduced_levels>=1` via `arc_solver_kit.reproduce()`, writes `complete_e3_tr87_ft09_partial` when both available games complete their bounded explore-verify-plan attempts without a reproduced L1, or records `blocked_offline_env_missing_<game>` for any missing per-game fixture while continuing the other game. A successful run MUST set `new_levels_reproduced>=1`, preserve exactly one `per_game_scorecard` row for each of `tr87` and `ft09`, set `verifier_is_oracle=true`, preserve both `world_model_paths`, set `submitted_to_leaderboard=false`, and compute the reproducibility checksum from the world-model hashes, per-game plans, reproduction-gate results, verifier rounds, and random seed. A partial run MUST set unsolved games to `offline_reproduced=false`, preserve each available game's world-model path and hash, persist the best verifier accuracy, and record each residual mismatch class as a missing-world-model-rule gap rather than claiming a solve.
